The '''2023–24 Liga 1''' (also known as the '''2023–24 [[Bank Rakyat Indonesia|BRI]] Liga 1''' for sponsorship reasons)<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bola.com |date=2023-06-26 |title=Resmi! BRI Kembali Jadi Sponsor Utama Liga 1 2023 / 2024 |url=https://www.bola.com/indonesia/read/5329474/resmi-bri-kembali-jadi-sponsor-utama-liga-1-2023-2024 |access-date=2023-06-26 |website=bola.com |language=id}}</ref> was the 7th season of [[Liga 1 (Indonesia)|Liga 1]] under its current name and the 14th season of the [[association football]], the top Indonesian [[association football|football]] league since its establishment in 2008. The season started on 1 July 2023 and ended on 31 May 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 May 2023 |title=Erick Thohir: Liga 1 Dimulai Pada 1 Juli 2023 Sampai 30 Mei 2024 |url=https://www.bolasport.com/read/313782005/erick-thohir-liga-1-dimulai-pada-1-juli-2023-sampai-30-mei-2024 |access-date=10 May 2023 |website=Bolasport.com |language=id}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 May 2024 |title=Resmi, Jadwal Championship Series Liga 1 |url=https://www.cnnindonesia.com/olahraga/20240503225326-142-1093791/resmi-jadwal-championship-series-liga-1 |access-date=3 May 2024 |website=CNN Indonesia |language=id}}</ref>

[[PSM Makassar]] were the reigning champions after outpacing their closest rivals, [[Persija Jakarta]] and [[Persib Bandung]] in the [[2022–23 Liga 1 (Indonesia)|2022–23 Liga 1]] season.<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2023 |title=PSM Makassar Juara Liga 1 |url=https://www.cnnindonesia.com/olahraga/20230331221743-142-932136/psm-makassar-juara-liga-1|access-date=18 June 2023|website=CNNIndonesia.com|language=id}}</ref>

== Overview ==
No teams were relegated last season due to the impact of the [[Kanjuruhan Stadium disaster]] which lead to the cancellation of [[2022–23 Liga 2 (Indonesia)|2022–23 Liga 2]]. Therefore, the 18 teams competing in the league remained the same as the preceding season.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Liga 1 2022/2023 Tanpa Promosi dan Degradasi |url=https://www.cnnindonesia.com/olahraga/20230112194651-142-899740/liga-1-2022-2023-tanpa-promosi-dan-degradasi |access-date=2023-01-12 |website=CNN Indonesia |language=id}}</ref>

Following the decision from the [[Asian Football Confederation|AFC]] Competitions Committee to increase the foreign players quota for AFC club competitions from the existing 3+1 quota to 5+1 (five players of any nationality and one from an AFC member association) that will take effect from the 2023–24 season onwards,<ref>{{cite web |title=Asian football panel approves strategic reforms; clubs can now sign six foreign players in all |url=https://www.daijiworld.com/news/newsDisplay?newsID=1032511 |website=daijiworld.com |access-date=23 December 2022 |language=en}}</ref> [[Football Association of Indonesia|PSSI]] increased the number of foreign players in Liga 1 clubs from four per team (with one of them coming from a member association of the AFC) to six per team with one of them coming from an [[ASEAN]] country.<ref>{{cite web |title=Aturan Pemain Asing 5+1 Untungkan Klub Indonesia di Kancah Asia |url=https://wartakota.tribunnews.com/2023/05/31/aturan-pemain-asing-51-untungkan-klub-indonesia-di-kancah-asia |website=wartakota.tribunnews.com |access-date=31 May 2023 |language=id}}</ref>

