== Foreign players ==
Following the decision from the [[Asian Football Confederation|AFC]] Competitions Committee to increase the foreign players quota for AFC club competitions from the existing 3+1 quota to 5+1 (five players of any nationality and one from an AFC member association) that will take effect from the 2023–24 season onwards,<ref>{{cite web |title=Asian football panel approves strategic reforms; clubs can now sign six foreign players in all |url=https://www.daijiworld.com/news/newsDisplay?newsID=1032511 |access-date=23 December 2022 |website=daijiworld.com |language=en}}</ref> [[Football Association of Indonesia|PSSI]] increased the number of foreign players in Liga 1 clubs from four per team (with one of them coming from a member association of the AFC) to six per team with one of them coming from an [[ASEAN]] country.<ref>{{cite web |title=Aturan Pemain Asing 5+1 Untungkan Klub Indonesia di Kancah Asia |url=https://wartakota.tribunnews.com/2023/05/31/aturan-pemain-asing-51-untungkan-klub-indonesia-di-kancah-asia |access-date=31 May 2023 |website=wartakota.tribunnews.com |language=id}}</ref>

